# Pipeline query caches. Every networked stage is resumable by writing one file
# per SPARQL response here; they are regenerable, large, and say nothing the
# corpus does not already record.
#
# All EIGHT cache directories belong here, not three. The growth run to ~2,200
# films fills .cache-posters/ with roughly 190 MB of poster bytes and the other
# four with tens of thousands of small JSON files; leaving any of them tracked
# turns `git status` after a harvest into an unreadable wall and makes an
# accidental `git add -A` commit the whole thing. .cache/ is written by
# wikidata.js:20 (entity lookups, also used by enrich.js:141) and .cache-posters/
# by palette.py -- neither was covered before the growth run.
/atlas/pipeline/.cache/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-sparql/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-expand/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-posters/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-plots/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-views/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-axes/

# Generated seed expansion. Regenerable with:
#   node atlas/pipeline/expand-seeds.js --target N > atlas/pipeline/seeds-expansion.txt
# Force-add the seed list once a run has completed if a harvest is built from it.
/atlas/pipeline/seeds-expansion.txt
/atlas/pipeline/seeds-expansion.report.tsv

# Default-path build output (node atlas/app/build.js with no --out) and Python
# bytecode from palette runs. Both regenerable, neither reviewable.
/atlas/atlas.html
__pycache__/
/atlas/pipeline/.cache-enrich/

# Derived: `cat seeds.txt seeds-expansion.txt > seeds-all.txt`, regenerated at
# the top of every harvest (see pipeline/RUN.md stage 1). Committing it would
# create a second, staler copy of a list that already has two sources of truth,
# and the concatenation ORDER is load-bearing -- seeds.txt must come first so
# `psycho` stays Hitchcock. RUN.md is where that order is enforced, not here.
/atlas/pipeline/seeds-all.txt

# Local linked worktrees used to isolate reviewed feature work from active
# pipeline outputs in the main checkout.
/.worktrees/

# Screenshots from .claude/skills/run-film-atlas/driver.mjs
/.atlas-shots/

# Scratch probes written at the repo root by agents driving the app — the
# driver and its harness live in .claude/skills/run-film-atlas/, so anything
# loose up here is somebody's in-flight measurement, not a deliverable. They
# have to sit inside the repo because `playwright` will not resolve from /tmp.
/.probe*.mjs
/.atlas-*.mjs
/bench-tmp.mjs
/.atlas-films/
/.atlas-films-snap/
